      "writtenOn": "2026-11-11T11:56:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PUT can\u0027t report deleted. The subscription is scope `BASE` with no stream params, so `DataTreeCandidateSerializer.serialize` takes the `serializeData(rootPath, candidate.getRootNode(), ...)` branch: one `data-change-event` per notification, for `/network-topology` itself, and `modificationTypeToOperation` maps `WRITE` to created/updated, only `DELETE`/`DISAPPEARED` to deleted. A leftover topology only decides which of created or updated the PUT reports.\n\nYour fix is still better, so switched to waiting for two `data-changed-notification` elements, same reason the create assertion below now accepts an update as well (the Robot original chose between those two too, just by stream version instead).\n\nHowever there is one issue -\u003e leftover `netconf-notif` from an aborted run makes the PUT a no-op (nothing is sent and the wait times out where matching on `deleted` would have passed). \nI think it might be preferable for it to fail here?",
